It seems to me that this started happening when upgrading Angular to 9/10 and moving to Ivy compilation. As @JoostK pointed out, I only experience this on certain pages that extend another template page.

```
import { TemplatePage } from '../tpl/template.page';

@Component({
    selector: 'app-some-page',
    templateUrl: './some.page.html',
})
export class SomePage extends TemplatePage {
    ...
```

I still consider this a bug as JIT should work with Ivy as well, but a "work-around" (I'm actually quite happy with that as it seems be the default for new projects) is to add the option `"aot": true` to the normal build section of the `angular.json` file. AOT is then used for `ng-serve` as well and the error disappears.

```
{
  ...,
  "projects": {
    "app": {
    ...,
      "architect": {
        "build": {
        ...,
          "options": {
          ...,
            "aot": true
...
```
